{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "122", "x": 0.8965598059325655, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03718344267107032, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING", "x": 0.4020190803040029, "y": 0.15408409893928954, "w": 0.13046256798557843, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 1", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21282136174528735, "w": 0.2852801181661608, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Question 1 – 13, which are based on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24770780300198914, "w": 0.8271735059525476, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Reading Passage 1 below", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2783001540994327, "w": 0.2720515284266326, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Georgia O'Keeffe", "x": 0.39294831317231377, "y": 0.3504832261266211, "w": 0.2570180637690859, "h": 0.026142547029900542, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "For seven decades, Georgia O'Keeffe (1887-1986) was a major figure in American", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38888499939419446, "w": 0.8266879477713279, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "art. Remarkably, she remained independent from shifting art trends and her work", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4092057398681471, "w": 0.8261860881224533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "stayed true to her own vision, which was based on finding the essential, abstract", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.42952648034209984, "w": 0.8258811789098378, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "forms in nature. With exceptionally keen powers of observation and great finesse", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.44999554133140524, "w": 0.8263234715605517, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "with a paintbrush, she recorded subtle nuances of colour, shape, and light that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47034098931745255, "w": 0.8261641477823392, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "enlivened her paintings and attracted a wide audience.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4906617297914052, "w": 0.5590863355459244, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Born in 1887 near Sun Prairie, Wisconsin to cattle breeders Francis and Ida", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5209203220079127, "w": 0.826621204026401, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "O'Keeffe, Georgia was raised on their farm along with her six siblings. By the time", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5413894207186106, "w": 0.8262511914681194, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "she graduated from high school in 1905, she had determined to make her way as", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5617101234711708, "w": 0.8260121032758466, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "an artist. She studied the techniques of traditional painting at the Art Institute of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5821792221818687, "w": 0.8266925613942492, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Chicago school (1905) and the Art Students League of New York (1907-8). After", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6024999249344289, "w": 0.8266731841779801, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "attending university and then training college, she became an art teacher and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6228206276869891, "w": 0.8261425150170862, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "taught in elementary schools, high schools, and colleges in Virginia, Texas, and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6432897641190795, "w": 0.8259901629357324, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "South Carolina from 1911 to 1918.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6636475470004779, "w": 0.337323271329317, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "During this period, O'Keeffe began to experiment with creating abstract", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6939061392169854, "w": 0.8261640452573853, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "compositions in charcoal, and produced a series of innovative drawings that led", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7142269551337231, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "her art in a new direction. She sent some of these drawings to a friend in New York,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7346959406802435, "w": 0.8267610480633908, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "who showed them to art collector and photographer Alfred Stieglitz in January", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7550167565969812, "w": 0.8261204721520182, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "1916.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7754857421435015, "w": 0.055279981295347426, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Stieglitz was impressed, and exhibited the drawings later that year at his gallery", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.805744409802794, "w": 0.8259029142000445, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "on Fifth Avenue, New York City, where the works of many avant-garde artists and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8260651502767468, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "photographers were introduced to the American public.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8463858907506995, "w": 0.5675523848688342, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "With Stieglitz's encouragement and promise of financial support, O'Keeffe arrived", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8766692282006942, "w": 0.8261862931723609, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in New York in June 1918 to begin a career as an artist. For the next three decades,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8971382891899995, "w": 0.8262294561779128, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Stieglitz vigorously promoted her work in twenty-two solo exhibitions and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9174590296639522, "w": 0.8265810142445095, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "numerous group installations. The two were married in 1924. The ups and downs", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9377797701379049, "w": 0.8261423099671786, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}